TASK 6 – LAST-MILE DELIVERY ROUTE OPTIMISATION
Travelling Salesperson Problem (TSP) Using Dynamic Programming – 9 Marks
6.1 – Model the optimisation problem
Aim: To find the minimum-cost delivery route using Dynamic Programming. The vehicle starts from the distribution hub, visits every delivery location exactly once, and returns to the hub.
Computational model
Component	Description
Input	Distribution hub, delivery locations and travel-cost matrix
Output	Minimum-cost route and its total travel cost
Objective	Minimise the total travel cost
Constraints	Start and finish at the hub; visit every delivery location exactly once

Why is the current location alone insufficient?

Suppose the vehicle is currently at location C.
- Route 1: Hub → A → C
- Route 2: Hub → B → C
Both routes end at C, but they have visited different locations. The remaining locations are also different.

Therefore, the algorithm must remember:
1. The locations already visited.
2. The current location.
3. The minimum cost of reaching that state.
This is why TSP uses a state containing both the visited-location set and the current location.
6.2 – Design the DP state
Let:
- \(S\) = set of delivery locations already visited.
- \(j\) = current delivery location.
- \(DP[S][j]\) = minimum cost of starting from the hub, visiting all locations in \(S\), and ending at location \(j\).
Let \(c(i,j)\) represent the travel cost from location \(i\) to location \(j\). The hub is represented by 0.
Base condition
When only one delivery location \(j\) has been visited:
\[
DP[\{j\}][j]=c(0,j)
\]

This means the vehicle travels directly from the hub to location \(j\).
Recurrence relation
For a set \(S\) containing more than one location:
\[
DP[S][j]=
\min_{k\in S,\ k\ne j}
\left(DP[S-\{j\}][k]+c(k,j)\right)
\]

Explanation:
- Consider every possible previous location \(k\).
- Remove the current location \(j\) from the visited set.
- Add the travel cost from \(k\) to \(j\).
- Choose the minimum-cost option.
Final solution
After visiting every delivery location, the vehicle must return to the hub.
\[
\boxed{
\text{Minimum Cost}=
\min_{j\in S_{\text{all}}}
(DP[S_{\text{all}}][j]+c(j,0))
}
\]

The algorithm also stores the previous location for every state so that the complete optimal route can be reconstructed.
