6.5 – Investigate the state-space growth
Dynamic Programming avoids calculating the same partial route repeatedly. However, it must still consider many different subsets of locations.

For \(n\) delivery locations:
- Number of DP states: \(n \times 2^{n-1}\)
- Time complexity: \(O(n^2 2^n)\)
- Space complexity: \(O(n 2^n)\)
Benchmark code
